Factorio AI includes third-party code:

game/client/
  The Windows and common parts of factorio-mcp by czp3009, https://github.com/czp3009/factorio-mcp (our fork's branch
  pilot as of commit e460220, 2026-11-07, which added player_action, memory_read and two world_query read forms). The
  upstream repository has no licence file; the code and its documents (tools.md, AGENTS.md, development.md, kept in
  game/client/) are used with the author's permission, relayed to us, on the condition of attribution. This project
  grants no licence to that code. Changes: Kotlin package renamed to factorioai.client, program renamed to
  factorio-ai-client.exe with factorio_ai_bridge.dll, environment variables renamed to FACTORIO_AI_CLIENT_*, the
  Linux target and npm packaging removed, local.properties generated by game/client/setup.ts.

commands/cli/
  The fh command line (compiled host/*.js) from factorio-ai-party's vendor/factorio-harness (same commit as below), MIT
  License (commands/cli/LICENSE). Changes: the --bot name rule relaxed to [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,31} (bot names are
  model names). Our broker (commands/broker.ts) speaks its FH_SOCKET protocol; the command name stays fh because the
  reference manuals the models read use it.

training/manuals/ref/
  The reference manuals the models read with `./fh help TOPIC` (analysis, building, circuits-settings, movement-combat,
  moving-items, space-age, team, waits-queues, index.md, topics.tsv) are copied from factorio-ai-party agent/ref (commit
  a9a5556a, 2026-11-04; MIT License, see training/manuals/ref/LICENSE), unchanged except stream-people.md left out.

core/brains/hooks/
  permit.ts ports the Bash permit rules of factorio-ai-party tools/permit.py and the examples of tools/test_permit.py
  (test/permit.test.ts); context.ts and hook.ts port the Claude Code parts of tools/context.py, agent/compact.md and
  agent/context.tsv (same repository and licence as below). Changes: our own tokenizer (stricter: word-initial # only,
  unknown operators rejected, for-lists and redirect targets checked, Windows paths), our command whitelist, the wait
  rules (sleepVerdict), the read guard, lower compaction points.

game/mod/factorio-ai-harness/
  The agent-harness mod from factorio-ai-party by Nick Winter, https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party
  (vendor/factorio-harness as of commit a9a5556a, 2026-11-04; MIT License, see game/mod/factorio-ai-harness/LICENSE), itself a
  fork of factorio-harness by Carson Burke, https://github.com/CarsonBurke/factorio-harness (MIT License).
  Changes: renamed to factorio-ai-harness; ported to Factorio 2.1 (compat21.lua, defines.inventory aliases, rewritten fluidbox /
  category reads, helpers.create_profiler, a require cache so modules can be loaded as plain files, UTF-8 safe reply truncation,
  relaxed bot name rule). In this project the same Lua also runs outside the game (game/offgame/) on top of a fake game API fed
  by process memory reads; the in-game copy is only used by tests as ground truth.
  game/mod/factorio-ai-harness/rates.lua ports formulas from RateCalculator v3.3.8 by Caleb Heuer (raiguard), MIT License,
  https://codeberg.org/raiguard/RateCalculator (noted in the file).


# 第二版 (factorio-pilot) 整目录搬来的部分, 原 NOTICE 照录 (2026-11-08)

Factorio Pilot includes third-party code:

src/io/ (mcp.ts, timeline.ts, controls.ts, czp-read.ts, czp-drive.ts and the world_query / input / ui_action calls around them), docs/io-client.md
  Built on factorio-mcp by czp3009, https://github.com/czp3009/factorio-mcp : the online client path drives the game through
  his MCP server, and these modules follow his tools.md. The upstream repository has no licence file; his code and docs are used
  with the author's permission, relayed to us, on the condition of attribution. npm run setup downloads a build of our fork
  https://github.com/Mkdms/factorio-mcp (branch pilot, see its FORK.md), which adds player_action, memory_read and a few read
  forms. It is not part of this repository and this project grants no licence to it.

knowledge/blueprints/community/
  Brian's Blueprints by bcwhite-code, https://github.com/bcwhite-code/brians-blueprints , CC0 1.0 (knowledge/blueprints/community/LICENSE).
  Migrated to Factorio 2.1 with that repository's own tools; each blueprint's source is in knowledge/blueprints/index.jsonl.

npm run setup also fetches factorio-ai-party by Nick Winter, https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party (MIT), at a fixed commit, into
lab-data/vendor/ (the shift brief, reference manuals and the ./fh command line). It is not copied into this repository.

mods/agent-harness/
  From factorio-harness by Carson Burke, https://github.com/CarsonBurke/factorio-harness
  (commit bcc2e9d, 2026-09-26), MIT License; see mods/agent-harness/LICENSE.
  Changes: ported to Factorio 2.1 (info.json, compat21.lua and the call sites that used
  LuaEntity::fluidbox, LuaEntity::neighbours, LuaRecipe::category and the removed furnace /
  assembling machine inventory defines). Resource hand-mining through timed mine_entity is taken
  from the factorio-ai-party fork (https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party, MIT).
  mods/agent-harness/rates.lua ports formulas from RateCalculator v3.3.8 by Caleb Heuer
  (raiguard), MIT License, https://codeberg.org/raiguard/RateCalculator (noted in the file).

mods/agent-harness-party/
  The factorio-harness fork from factorio-ai-party by Nick Winter, https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party
  (vendor/factorio-harness as of commit a9a5556a, 2026-11-04; last harness change 83aea242), MIT License; see mods/agent-harness-party/LICENSE.
  Generated by tools/port-party-harness.py: renamed to agent-harness-party, ported to Factorio 2.1 (compat21.lua,
  defines.inventory aliases, rewritten fluidbox / category reads, resource paths), guest permission group disabled.

src/play/claude-stream.ts (play:run --stream) and readPlanUsage() in src/play/quota.ts (npm run play:quota)
  Adapted from OpenMausBot by Milind Soni and OpenMausBot contributors, https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot
  (commit 9649348, 2026-11-03), Apache License 2.0. Taken from server/drivers/claude.ts: the long-lived
  `claude -p --input-format stream-json --replay-user-messages` session, folding a message written mid-turn into the
  running turn, holding a `result` while a written message has not been echoed yet (2 s grace), and reading
  total_cost_usd as cumulative. Taken from server/plan-usage.ts: the plan-usage request (api/oauth/usage with the
  anthropic-beta oauth header, the token from .credentials.json) and its window format. Re-implemented in our code;
  changes: one class per session, the request goes through HTTPS_PROXY (https.Agent proxyEnv), Chinese messages.

src/play/digest.ts (play:run --kit party: the supervisor's per-owner factory digest)
  Ported from factorio-ai-party by Nick Winter, https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party (e98eb874, 2026-11-02), MIT License:
  tools/factory_digest.py (owners, current, moved, delta, delta_messages) and tools/stream/hauling.py (shift_rows, haul_line), to
  TypeScript. Changes: Chinese text; with no board claims the facts go by role; shortage and full-output facts carry up to three
  positions; full output only counts while some machine is short; factsFromHealth falls back to our own health scan when the
  harness survey cache has expired.

src/play/permit.ts (the brain's PreToolUse hook: pre-approve shell commands built only from allowed programs)
  Ported from factorio-ai-party by Nick Winter, https://github.com/nwinter/factorio-ai-party (7ff35170, 2026-11-03), MIT License:
  tools/permit.py (allowed programs, lists / pipes / loops / conditionals, plain $name variables, redirects only to /dev/null
  or relative workspace paths) and the examples in tools/test_permit.py, to TypeScript. Changes (no Claude Code sandbox on
  Windows, so stricter): a bash-like tokenizer instead of shlex (a # inside a word, |& and for-list words used as redirect
  targets no longer slip through), no python3 / sleep / rg, options that write or hang refused (sort -o, uniq OUTPUT,
  tail -f, date -s, printf -v), Windows drive and UNC paths count as absolute, cd into the agent's own directory accepted,
  while / until loops and sleeps inside loops refused with a reason.

src/play/partykit.ts, src/play/fh-shim.ts (play:run --kit party)
  Use factorio-ai-party's agent kit at run time from a local clone (not copied into this repository): the brief
  (agent/PLAYBOOK.md, agent/compact.md, agent/harness-claude.md, agent/time-realtime.md via tools/brief.py), the
  reference topics (agent/ref), tools/describe-lines.py and the host CLI (vendor/factorio-harness, built locally).
  coopText() in partykit.ts is adapted from agent/coop.md, and src/play/brief-zh.md is a Chinese translation of the
  generated AGENTS.md (agent/PLAYBOOK.md, coop.md, harness-claude.md, compact.md). By Nick Winter, MIT License.

app/src/index.css, app/src/components/ (the desktop UI, Tauri)
  Adapted from OpenGrokBot by wolfqing and OpenGrokBot contributors, https://github.com/wolfqing/OpenGrokBot
  (commit d3de545, 2026-11-02), MIT License; see app/third-party/OpenGrokBot-LICENSE. Taken from web/src/index.css:
  the dark theme tokens, sidebar rows with avatar state dots and pending badges, thread rows, the collapsible activity
  chip, the amber "needs you" card, the composer and the right-hand panel; and the layout of web/src/components/
  Sidebar.tsx, Thread.tsx and ActivityChip.tsx. Re-implemented in our code; changes: Chinese UI and fonts, the right
  panel shows game readings, the steps fold the Bash commands and results from the brain's stream-json, times only
  after a pause, unused chips left out.

app/src/theme.ts, app/src/useTheme.ts (light / dark theme of the desktop UI)
  Adapted from OpenMausBot, Copyright 2026 Milind Soni and OpenMausBot contributors,
  https://github.com/milind-soni/OpenMausBot (commit 9649348, 2026-11-03), Apache License 2.0; see
  app/third-party/OpenMausBot-LICENSE. Taken from src/lib/skins.ts: following the OS between a light and a dark look
  with matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"), "system" as the default choice, keeping the choice in localStorage
